# Full ordering at the final code — run F

`bun run test:e2e`, stock config (per-test timeout 30 s, retries 0, workers 1),
lane-private ports 4341/5193 (vault 4409/5184), listeners on those ports killed
and `.dokan-port` removed first.

```
Running 93 tests using 1 worker
...
  x  28 tests\e2e\expense-reports.spec.ts:144:1 › profit report reconciles revenue, COGS, expenses, withdrawals and the result (12.9s)
...
  1 failed
  92 passed (14.9m)
```

The single failure is in the **shared `signIn` preamble**, before any line this
round changes:

```
Error: expect(locator).toBeVisible() failed
Locator: getByTestId('dashboard-page')
Expected: visible
Timeout: 5000ms
       at signIn (tests/e2e/auth-helpers.ts:55:77)
```

`dashboard-page` is the dashboard's root `<section>`, rendered unconditionally
(`apps/web/src/pages/dashboard.tsx:116`) — it is not behind a query, so a missing
section means the route did not mount inside 5 s, i.e. the Vite dev server had
not finished compiling the route under load. The same wait flaked in
`01-empty-states.spec.ts` at 20:0x and passes on every quiet run.

The test's own body (including the new end-state assertions) passes when the spec
is run alone on the same code:

```
bunx playwright test tests/e2e/expense-reports.spec.ts --grep "reconciles revenue"
  ok 1 tests\e2e\expense-reports.spec.ts:144:1 › profit report reconciles ... (20.1s)
  1 passed (43.5s)
```

`debts.spec.ts`, `96-returns-supplier-action.spec.ts`, `01-empty-states.spec.ts`
and `00-onboarding.spec.ts` all passed in this run (tests 1–6, 14–15, 27).

Two other attempts at this commit did not produce a result at all: one aborted
after 5 tests with exit 255 (process killed, no Playwright error) and one exited
1 before running anything, both with leftover servers from the aborted attempt.
Recorded rather than hidden; see `full-suite-flakes.log`.
